<title>USA: Lockheed Martin unit wins Post Office pact.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin unit wins Post Office pact.</headline>
<dateline>OWEGO, N.Y. 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp said on Tuesday that a unit had been awarded a contract worth more than $50 million to deploy the first production units of a computer-controlled material handling system for the U.S. Postal Service.</p>
<p>The program has a potential value of $1 billion through the year 2000.</p>
<p>The contract was awarded to Lockheed Martin Federal Systems.</p>
